From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: devaOS RF35H <devaos@rf35h>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 15:33:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Linux: OpenGL ES 3.2 renderer (tag gles), no GTK (tag
 nodialog)

- render_gles32.go/font_gles32.go build with "android || gles"; on
  desktop Linux the GL function pointers come from SDL (EGL), see
  util_gles_desktop.go. selectRenderer accepts "OpenGL ES 3.2" when the
  renderer is compiled in and falls back to OpenGL 3.3 otherwise.
- rendererAvailable() + Lua isRendererAvailable(): the options menu
  lists only the renderers compiled into the binary, and "default
  values" picks OpenGL ES 3.2 when it is available.
- Dialogs split out of util_desktop.go: GTK (default) or stderr with
  the "nodialog" tag, for devices without a desktop (no GTK needed).
---
 external/script/options.lua | 12 +++++++++---
 src/font_gles32.go          |  2 +-
 src/render_gles32.go        |  2 +-
 src/script.go               |  9 +++++++++
 src/util_android.go         |  4 ++++
 src/util_desktop.go         | 29 ++++++++++++++++++++---------
